messages:
rachel: quick sync from today's arch check-in: interface boundaries between query service and authz service are still fuzzy. proposing explicit minimal interface: VerifyRequest(user, tenant, resource, action, ctx) -> ALLOW/DENY + reasons.
tom: we should avoid opaque reasons in hot path; include only a short code and optional trace id to get more details async.
jyoti: do we need resource normalization in query service or authz service? duplication might cost CPU.\arachel: normalize in query service to keep authz service simple. query knows tenant semantics and can map panel_id -> resource tuple.
tom: how about caching keys and TTLs? Keep them deterministic: key = sha256(tenant||resource||action). TTL by policy complexity heuristics.
jyoti: fallback for shared resources with cross-tenant references still needs sync. maybe introduce VerifyBatch for multi-row checks to amortize.
\rachel: agreed. add VerifyBatch API returning list of codes aligned with inputs. backpressure necessary: limit batch size to 128.
tom: perf: single verify ~3ms; batch of 64 reduces per-item to ~0.6ms in our bench (shared compute). downside: bigger blast radius for retries.
ops-bot: Recommend: circuit-breaker on verify latency > 250ms per request for >1% of requests.
rachel: authz service should not be a single point: run in regional clusters and add short-lived cache in query service for 1s to handle brief spikes.
jyoti: +1. also add strict quota per-tenant to avoid noisy neighbors.
\rtom: sketch proto:
```
service Authz {
  rpc Verify(Request) returns (Response);
  rpc VerifyBatch(BatchRequest) returns (BatchResponse);
}

message Request {
  string user = 1;
  string tenant = 2;
  string resource = 3;
  string action = 4;
  map<string,string> ctx = 5;
}
```

rachel: include response codes: ALLOW, DENY, INDETERMINATE, FALLBACK_REQUIRED. FALLBACK_REQUIRED signals query service to perform local sync check.
jyoti: doc update: add clear exemptions when action==read_metadata -> allow cheaper checks.
ops-bot: Canary note: Authz API contract v2 -> rolling for 14 days across regions.
rachel: next steps: PR with proto, perf numbers, and a migration plan for older clients. aim to land proto in 2 weeks.
tom: also add integration test harness that can simulate tenant quota exhaustion.
